    <briefdescription>
<para>Represent a subset of the particles being optimized. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Domino acts by dividing the particles being changed into subsets and optimizing the subsets independently. Each subset is represented using a <ref refid="classIMP_1_1domino_1_1Subset" kindref="compound">Subset</ref> class. These classes, like the <ref refid="classIMP_1_1domino_1_1Assignment" kindref="compound">Assignment</ref> classes, simply store a constant list (in this case of particles). The list is stored in sorted order. Their interface is more or less that of a constant vector in C++ or a constant list in Python. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
